# Terminal status block (D-61 / D-66)

**Authority:** Dan 2026-08-05 (D-61); amended Dan 2026-08-08 (D-66). Platform parity (D-32).
**SSOT:** this file only. Other rules point here — do not restate the four-status schema elsewhere.

## Trigger (mandatory)

Any turn with agent action — code/config/product edits or ships, deploy, verify, investigate, harness/rules work, or any tool use that changes repo/runtime state.

Skip only for pure one-line Q&A with no tool actions and no state change.

## Exactly one terminal block — always last

The reply must end with **exactly one** of the four blocks below. **Nothing may appear after it** (no gotchas, no verifier lines, no shell notes, no postscripts).

Do **not** emit multiple DONE/BLOCKED/FAILED/PARTIAL summaries. Do **not** treat stray shell/job completion notifications as the authoritative task status.

Final status must reflect the **actual task outcome**. A mid-turn shell failure does **not** mean **FAILED** if the task later completed successfully by another route.

### DONE — finished

```text
DONE — finished
What I did: <1–2 sentence summary>
Your action: <exact next action, or "Nothing needed">
```

Use when the requested/approved scope for this turn is complete. On substantive ships, **What I did** reuses the opening **What we did** (one shared summary).

**97 rule (D-47/D-69):** do **not** use DONE when confAfter < 97% — report actual confidence + uncertainty; prefer BLOCKED or PARTIAL (`confidence-gate.mdc`). ≥97% does not waive D-38/D-60/ship gates.

If production verification was part of the requested task and is still outstanding → do **not** use DONE.

Phased work: if the **approved phase** is fully complete and the agent intentionally stops before the next phase → DONE is OK; put the next approval ask in **Your action** (not a second status block).

### BLOCKED — needs input

```text
BLOCKED — needs input
What I did: <completed work summary>
Blocked by: <specific blocker>
Your action: <exact required input>
```

Use when continuing requires Dan (approve / secret / decide / wait). **Your action** must be a concrete Dan step — never `Nothing needed`.

Stopping for approval/input → **BLOCKED**, not DONE with a soft ask.

### FAILED — stopped

```text
FAILED — stopped
What I did: <completed work summary>
Failure: <specific failure>
Your action: <recommended next step>
```

Use when the task stopped unsuccessfully and is not merely waiting on Dan input (that is BLOCKED).

### PARTIAL — some work completed

```text
PARTIAL — some work completed
What I did: <completed portion>
Remaining: <unfinished portion>
Your action: <next step>
```

Use when agent-owned scope remains unfinished and work could continue without waiting on Dan. **Not** for deferred unrelated work. Waiting on Dan → **BLOCKED**, not PARTIAL.

## Idle string

Canonical: **`Nothing needed`** (on DONE when Dan has no next step). Do not use `Nothing needed from you.`

## Relation

- Complements `composer-orchestrator.mdc` § Completion report (opening **What we did** on ships) — does **not** replace verifier evidence lines, which appear **before** this block.
- **MANUAL TEST FOR DAN (D-78):** SSOT detail in `composer-orchestrator.mdc` § Completion report. When required (user-observable product behavior shipped/repaired), that section appears **before** this terminal block (and before any cloud ARCHIVE/KEEP marker). Missing required section = incomplete completion report — **not** a fifth status. When the full section applies, DONE **`Your action`** points at it (not `Nothing needed`). Automated verify PASS does not waive D-78.
- Supersedes the old D-61 form `DONE — finished | blocked` (status as a DONE suffix). Statuses are mutually exclusive first lines only.
